Package: limn
Type: Package
Title: A Projection Engine for Distributional Forecasting
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person(given = "Craig P.", family = "Hutton",
                  role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
                  email = "craig.hutton@gmail.com")
Description: Predictive distributions, forecasts, proper scoring rules,
    calibration, cross-validation and model comparison for models fitted by
    'illume'. A prediction is a mixture over draws of the fitted parameters,
    so its intervals carry the fit's own uncertainty, and every score is
    computed from that mixture rather than from simulated responses. How the
    random effects enter a prediction is always named, never assumed: a unit
    seen in the fit, a new one, a typical one, or the population average.
    Cross-validation follows the structure of the data, with grouped folds for
    new units and rolling origins for forecasts, and model comparisons carry
    standard errors clustered the same way. 'limn' is the third package in a
    family, after 'illumex' for exploration and 'illume' for inference.
